Author: pekorali <30273565+pekorali@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Wed Oct 21 08:32:43 2026 +0300

    feat(kscan): filter ghost keys of a diodeless matrix
    
    In a matrix without diodes three keys forming an L shape create a conducting
    path that makes a fourth key read as pressed. The sets {W,S,D} and {W,S,D,E}
    are electrically identical, so the ghost cannot be detected by any digital
    scan - the driver now picks the most plausible interpretation instead:
    
      * a cell that only appeared because a chain of three pressed keys just got
        completed is dropped as a ghost,
      * keys already reported as pressed are never dropped,
      * dropped ghosts are remembered until the key is released.
    
    The behaviour is behind CONFIG_ZMK_KSCAN_GPIO_MATRIX_HIZ_GHOST_FILTER (on by
    default); setting it to n shows the raw matrix again.

